Build GSocket without IP-level socket options.

zedBSD's network stack implements no IP-level socket options (no IP_TTL,
multicast loopback/TTL or group membership, nor their IPv6 counterparts),
no SOCK_SEQPACKET and no FIONREAD, and its C library defines neither
SOMAXCONN nor the BSD IN_MULTICAST() macro.  When the options are absent,
the time-to-live and multicast calls report G_IO_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED (the
getters keep their existing warning-and-zero behaviour), a
sequenced-packet socket cannot be created, g_socket_get_available_bytes()
reports -1 on a stream socket, SOMAXCONN falls back to the traditional 128
for the listen-backlog property, and IN_MULTICAST() gets its usual
definition.  The locals and the interface-address helper that only the
group membership code uses are left out with it, so the build stays free
of unused and uninitialized warnings.  Platforms that define the options
are compiled exactly as before.

--- a/gio/gsocket.c
+++ b/gio/gsocket.c
